      "explanation": "<p>Consider a spherical shell of radius r and small thickness dr.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2015 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Rotational Motion Question 63 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0ylxcla/78ae1c7b-42c4-4ffd-9bda-3ec88b712795/032da1e0-a7ee-11ec-82ec-9768dcc201cf/file-1l0ylxclb.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The volume of the shell is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.579ex\" height=\"1.937ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBo